## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Build and delivery

  req F-1.1:
    when: the site is built
    then: the output is static files, built by Astro with Starlight, with no server code

  req F-1.2:
    when: a reader searches
    then: Pagefind answers from an index built with the site, with no third-party service

  req F-1.3:
    when: a reader moves between pages in a browser that supports it
    then: a cross-document view transition keeps the header and sidebar in place, with no client router

  req F-1.4:
    when: the site is deployed
    then: it ships in the dxos.org build: the landing page at `/echo`, the written and planned pages under
          `/docs/echo`, and the agent routes under `/echo`
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Brand and visual style

  req F-2.1:
    when: the site needs a color
    then: it reads a CSS variable generated from the brand palette, never a literal

  req F-2.2:
    when: text renders
    then: headings and body use DM Sans, labels and code use DM Mono, and Sharp Sans appears only
          in a logotype

  req F-2.3:
    when: the site shows a logo, icon, font or background
    then: the file comes from `@dxos/brand`, and is not copied into this package

  req F-2.4:
    when: a surface renders
    then: it is flat, with a ground, one tinted surface and hairlines; no surface has a shadow,
          a raised edge or an inset edge

  req F-2.5:
    when: a code sample renders
    then: it sits on the tinted surface inside a hairline frame, with numbered lines and a rule beside
          the numbers except in a side-by-side comparison, and a titled sample shows its title as a tab; a syntax theme colors it with a
          contrast of at least 4.5:1 for every token, and long lines wrap

  req F-2.13:
    when: a reader is not pointing at a token in a code sample
    then: the token carries no underline; its compiler hover card shows on hover

  req F-2.6:
    when: a table renders
    then: every row shares fixed column tracks, and content wraps inside its track rather than
          widening a column

  req F-2.7:
    when: single-line interface text would overflow (nav item, breadcrumb, chip)
    then: it does not wrap; it truncates with an ellipsis

  req F-2.8:
    when: the reader's system or theme picker selects dark
    then: the Graphite ground applies, with cyan replacing blue as the accent

  req F-2.9:
    when: the ECHO mark renders on a light ground
    then: it uses the ECHO product hue; on a dark ground it uses the foreground color, since the
          product hue falls below 3:1 there

  req F-2.10:
    when: the reader prefers reduced motion
    then: hover and view transitions do not animate

  req F-2.11:
    when: the landing page renders
    then: its hero shows the ECHO background art from `@dxos/brand`

  req F-2.12:
    when: a list renders
    then: its text and markers set `tabular-nums` and stay in DM Sans; the brand's DM Sans has no
          tabular figures, so digits remain proportional until the font gains them

```

```mdl
feat F-3: Checked code samples

  req F-3.1:
    when: a page shows code longer than one line
    then: the code comes from a file in the snippets directory, included by region

  req F-3.2:
    when: the site is built or typechecked
    then: every snippet compiles against the workspace packages of this commit, so an API change
          that breaks a sample fails the build

  req F-3.3:
    when: a snippet prints a result in a comment
    then: a test runs that snippet against an in-memory database and asserts the result

  req F-3.4:
    when: a reader hovers an identifier in a sample on a docs page
    then: its compiler-inferred type appears
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Accuracy

  req F-4.1:
    when: a page states a guarantee about ECHO's behavior
    then: it links the spec item that states it, as `org.dxos.echo.query#F-2`

  req F-4.2:
    when: a reference page lists a member
    then: the member is an export of the module in this commit; the reference is generated from
          the TypeScript declarations, not from the spec's `module` blocks, which have drifted
          from the code

  req F-4.3:
    when: the spec's own review marks a cited item as diverged or partial
    then: the page's Limits section says so
```

```mdl
feat F-5: The spec drives the site map

  req F-5.1:
    when: the site is built
    then: the order, groups and labels of the ECHO section of the docs sidebar come from the `page` blocks
          in this document

  req F-5.2:
    when: a `page` block has status `planned`
    then: the page exists as a stub that shows its summary and its template's parts, with a
          planned badge in the sidebar

  req F-5.3:
    when: a `page` block has status `spike` or `done`
    then: a content file exists at its route, and the build fails if it does not
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Reading by agents

  req F-6.1:
    when: an agent fetches `/echo/llms.txt`
    then: it receives the site map, each page with its summary and link, in the llms.txt format

  req F-6.2:
    when: an agent fetches a written page's route with `.md` appended
    then: it receives the page as Markdown, with snippet includes replaced by their code
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Relationship to dxos.org

  req F-7.1:
    when: a reader is on any dxos.org docs page
    then: the header shows the DXOS logo, linking home, and the dxos.org nav (Home, ECHO, Composer,
          Plugins, Blog, Docs); the footer links the same pages, the ECHO, Composer and HALO docs,
          GitHub and Discord

  req F-7.2:
    when: a reader looks for ECHO material on dxos.org
    then: every ECHO page is a page of this site map; no other ECHO guide remains

  req F-7.3:
    when: a dxos.org Webflow page renders
    then: its nav and footer link `/echo`, and the home page's ECHO card links `/echo`

  req F-7.4:
    when: a reader is on `/echo`
    then: it has the dxos.org Webflow nav and footer, with no docs header, search or sidebar, and its
          actions lead into `/docs/echo`; the Webflow styles sit in a cascade layer above the theme's global
          reset and below its base, component and utility layers, and stop at each embedded component, so the
          page keeps its typography and code samples and embedded components keep their styling

  req F-7.5:
    when: a reader is on `/echo`
    then: it shows live demos, in order: a collaborative editor, a table and board over one data set, a graph
          explorer, and an architecture diagram; each runs two peers, Alice and Bob, in one space in the page,
          shows one or both, and has a switch per peer that takes it offline
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Live playground

  desc: |
    A browser playground runs a real ECHO database in the page, with two peers side by side, so a
    reader can make a conflicting edit and watch the merge. Planned; the spike does not build it.

  req F-8.1:
    when: a reader edits a sample in the playground
    then: the code runs against an in-memory database in the page, with no server

feat F-9: Diagrams as canvas applications

  desc: |
    Each diagram is a stand-alone `plugin-canvas` application. `/echo` shows Composer's architecture
    this way; the docs pages still render their diagrams as static images.

  req F-9.1:
    when: a page shows a diagram
    then: the diagram is a stand-alone `plugin-canvas` application

feat F-10: Live schema forms

  desc: |
    A section on Schema shows a live `react-ui-form` form. Planned; the spike does not build it.

  req F-10.1:
    when: a reader opens the section on Schema
    then: it shows a live form rendered with `react-ui-form`

feat F-11: Graph visualizations

  desc: |
    A section on the graph shows visualizations from `react-ui-graph` and `plugin-explorer`.
    `/echo` shows the `plugin-explorer` graph of a demo space; the docs section is planned.

  req F-11.1:
    when: a reader opens the section on the graph
    then: it shows visualizations from `react-ui-graph` and `plugin-explorer`

feat F-12: Real-time editor demo

  desc: |
    A section on real time shows a `react-ui-editor` demo. `/echo` shows it with two peers editing one
    document; the docs section is planned.

  req F-12.1:
    when: a reader opens the section on real time
    then: it shows a demo built with `react-ui-editor`

feat F-13: Chat and hierarchical feeds demo

  desc: |
    A demo shows chat and hierarchical feeds with `plugin-assistant`. Planned; the spike does not
    build it.

  req F-13.1:
    when: a reader opens the demo
    then: it shows chat and hierarchical feeds with `plugin-assistant`

feat F-14: Upfront motivation

  desc: |
    The site says why ECHO exists before it says how ECHO works.

  req F-14.1:
    when: a reader opens the landing page or Why ECHO?
    then: before any other argument, it gives the motivation for agents and agent memory, the rationale
          for being introspectable, and the role of tying together data from external sources, and it
          says that ECHO is the data model that apps (plugins) code against

  req F-14.2:
    when: the motivation shows code
    then: the sample is checked like every other sample [F-3], and each claim about an agent names the
          skill or operation that does it
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: A sample that stops compiling fails the build.
  given: a snippet that calls `Obj.make`
  when: the signature of `Obj.make` changes incompatibly
  then: the site's build and typecheck fail, and the typecheck names the snippet
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: A planned page is visible, and marked.
  given: a `page` block with status `planned`
  when: the site is built
  then: the sidebar shows the page with a planned badge, and its route renders the stub template
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Both themes meet the contrast floor.
  given: the brand palette and syntax themes
  when: the theme script runs
  then: body text on the ground is at least 7:1, muted text and code tokens are at least 4.5:1, and
        the script fails otherwise
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: A phone can read the site.
  given: a 375 pixel wide viewport
  when: any spike page renders
  then: the page does not scroll sideways, and every line of a code sample is visible without scrolling
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: An agent gets the code, not the include.
  given: a page that includes a snippet
  when: an agent fetches the page's `.md` route
  then: the body contains the snippet's code and no `<Snippet` tag
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: ECHO has a detailed technical developer website.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The site complements the dxos.org website, which is coded in the dxos repository.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The site uses the design system from the `dxos/studio` repository.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-2]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: The site uses the state of the art.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1, F-3, F-6]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: The site's content sections are similar to the Effect page "Why Effect?".
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [why-echo]
  source: https://effect.website/docs/v4/getting-started/why-effect
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The site is a new private package built with Astro and Starlight, apart from the dxos.org build. Fills in [D-1] and [D-2].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1]
  why: |
    The dxos.org build already runs Astro and Starlight, so the repo's catalog, moon tasks and
    deploy path apply unchanged. A separate package lets the theme replace Starlight's look without
    touching the Webflow pages on dxos.org.
  rejected:
    - New pages inside the dxos.org build: its theme and sidebar serve Composer and HALO too.
    - A custom Astro docs shell: it would rebuild search, sidebar, table of contents and pagination.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: Depth marks what can be pressed; reading material stays flat. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-2.3, F-2.4]
  why: The kit is tuned for slides and social media. Soft shadows behind long text and tables lower contrast and add noise.
  rejected:
    - Neumorphism on every surface: paragraphs in raised cards read as slides.
    - The brand kit's flat hairline grid alone: it drops the kit's most distinct feature.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Accent stays the kit's blue in light and cyan in dark; the ECHO product hue marks only the logo. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-2.8, F-2.9]
  why: The product hue `#96254f` has too little contrast on the dark ground to carry links.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Samples compile against the workspace, and hover types are a separate requirement. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3]
  why: The ECHO pages on dxos.org still describe `@dxos/client` flows that have moved, so correctness has to be mechanical.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: The reference is generated from TypeScript declarations, not from the `module` blocks of `org.dxos.echo`. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-4.2]
  why: The review of `org.dxos.echo` records members its `module` blocks list that the code lacks, such as `Obj.getDXN`.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: The `page` blocks of this spec generate the sidebar and the planned stubs. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-5]
  why: The plan is then visible in the running site, and the spec cannot drift from the navigation.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: The site map follows Effect's split of start here, learning path and core concepts, and adds guides, internals and reference. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [why-echo]
  why: ECHO readers need the sync and query internals that Effect's docs have no counterpart for.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Agents read the site through `/llms.txt` and a Markdown route per page. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-6]
  why: Coding agents are a main reader of developer docs, and rendered HTML costs them more to read.
```

```mdl
question Q-1: Where does the site live?
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
