```

```mdl
decision D-51: On `/echo` the Webflow layer sits above Tailwind's preflight and below the react-ui theme's base, component and utility layers. A copy of the preflight, scoped to the demos and to the menus and dialogs they portal outside the Webflow content, sits above the Webflow layer. Fills in [D-44].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-46
  affects: [F-7.4]
  why: With the Webflow layer lowest, the theme's global preflight reset the page's headings, nav and code frames; with it above the preflight, Webflow's element rules would reach inside a demo, so the demos get their own scoped reset.
  rejected:
    - Shadow DOM around each demo: portalled menus and dialogs render outside it, and the theme's tokens sit on `:root`.
    - Iframes: each demo would load its own page and copy of the theme.
```

```mdl
decision D-52: `/echo` has live demos, built as React islands from Composer plugin surfaces and sample-space templates with in-memory clients and peers, not iframes: a markdown editor, two peers by default, with cursors; the nested DXOS architecture diagram on a canvas; a table and a kanban board over the same data, one view per peer; and the explorer's force-directed graph, which shows a card for a node. Each demo has a toolbar to show one or two peers, its peers are created and joined in advance, and a per-peer offline switch is optional. Demos are easy to add and reorder.
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-7.5, F-9, F-11, F-12]
```

```mdl
decision D-53: On `/echo` the Webflow styles are scoped to stop at each demo and at what a demo portals outside the Webflow content. Fills in [D-51].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-7.4]
  why: Webflow class rules that share a name with a Tailwind utility reached into the demos: Webflow's `.grid` gives three columns and a 4rem gap, which laid a demo's toolbar beside its panes.
  rejected:
    - Renaming each colliding class: every plugin a demo adds brings classes that would need checking.
```

```mdl
decision D-54: Each demo runs two peers, Alice and Bob, each a Composer plugin app with its own in-memory client. Alice creates the space and seeds it from the demo's sample-space partial; Bob joins it by invitation; both join when the page opens, so showing the second peer is instant. A demo names the object each peer opens, and a peer can switch between a demo's objects. The online switch takes a peer's network offline, and its edits merge when it comes back. The page lists its demos by id, in order. Fills in [D-52].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-7.5]
  why: One space per demo keeps the demos independent, and a list of ids is the one place that adds or reorders a demo.
```

```mdl
decision D-55: The editor seeds a short checklist; the table, board and graph share six companies and their people; the diagram seeds Composer's architecture set, opening on its overview, read-only until a peer unlocks it. The board hides the column for companies with no status, and the graph opens a node's card on hover. Fills in [D-52].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-7.5, F-9, F-11]
  why: Composer's set is the nested architecture diagram the canvas plugin ships; every seeded company has a status, so that column stays empty; the explorer opens cards on hover, not on click.
```

```mdl
decision D-56: The architecture diagram demo opens with one peer.
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-7.5]
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext template
  uri: org.dxos.echo-site.template@1.0
  desc: A page format, as the ordered parts every page of that template has.
  fields:
    purpose: Prose
    parts: ProseList
```

```mdl
ext page
  uri: org.dxos.echo-site.page@1.0
  desc: One page of the site. The inline prose is its summary; the block's position sets its sidebar order.
  inline-prose: true
  fields:
    route: URI
    group: Prose
    template: ExtRef
    status: planned | spike | done
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext decision
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0
  desc: |
    One decision about the spec, attributed to exactly one actor. The inline prose is the decision
    itself, stated as what is now true, not as the edit that was made.
  fields:
    date: Date                  # YYYY-MM-DD, the day the decision was made
    by: ActorRef                # user:<handle> | agent:<name> — the decider
    for?: UserRef               # agent entries only: the person the agent acted for
    affects?: RefList           # block ids the decision constrains, e.g. [Scene, F-2.1]
    supersedes?: Identifier     # an earlier decision this one replaces
    why?: Prose                 # the reason; on a user entry, only a reason the person gave
    rejected?: ProseList        # alternatives considered and why they lost
    source?: URI                # PR, review comment, issue, or session where it was made
  inline-prose: true
```
